Z||000000||Will||06-24-2001||11:09 PM||||What I said above, and:<P>How would the handling of a Fiero stiff rear springs but a weaker rear bar compare to one with stock springs, but a stiffer rear bar?||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||06-24-2001||11:31 PM||||The swaybar will actually increase the outside spring's spring rate. If you have stiffer springs and smaller bar, you will actually reduce the effectiveness of the bar even more.<P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe (V6 & fastback conversion)<BR><B>You must be fast, cuz I was haulin' ass when I passed you!</B><p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 06-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||06-24-2001||11:37 PM||||You tend to loose some compliance with a huge rear bar,or in other words you give the right to break loose to any one tire hitting a bump.That's been my experience anyways.||||reg||1
